prayerPoint.description:
O God our Father,
blessed be your name forever, for you have delivered us.
We come again now to the cross where the Saviour bled;
we look again in faith to him.

Lord God, we see in your crucified Son a sacrifice for sin;
we see how you made him to be sin for us,
so that in him we might become the righteousness of God.
We are not our own;
we were bought with a price.

Lord Jesus, renew your grasp of us;
we surrender ourselves to you.
Mark us anew as your own possession,
that we may live for you now and forever. Amen.

O God, unsearchable depth of peace, boundless sea of love, fountain of blessing and giver of kindness, who sends peace to those who receive it;

Open to us today the sea of your love, and water us with the full streams of your grace. Make us children of quietness, and heirs of peace.

Kindle in us the fire of your love; plant in us reverence for you; strengthen our weakness by your power; bind us closely to you and to each other in one firm bond of unity; for the sake of Jesus Christ. Amen.

O God, Father of our Saviour Jesus Christ, whose name is great, whose nature is full of blessing, whose goodness never runs dry, God and Ruler of all things, blessed for ever; before whom stand thousands upon thousands, the hosts of holy angels and archangels;

Sanctify, O Lord, our souls and bodies and spirits, search our consciences, and cast out from us every evil thought, every base desire, all envy and pride, all anger and wrath, and all that is contrary to your holy will.

And grant us, O Lord, lover of all people, with a pure heart and a humble spirit, to call upon you, our holy God and Father in heaven. Amen.
